 "code": "mem = rlm.harness.create_memory(title='Continual ARC task-ce5ee053: move object toward separator and add color-8 line', content='Task-ce5ee053 solved. Input has a full separator line in color 2 and a distinct shape/object on one side. Move the entire foreground object toward the separator until its nearest bounding-box edge is adjacent to the separator (preserve its shape and orientation); remove the original placement. Then draw a full line of color 8 parallel to the separator immediately beyond the moved object on its far side (away from the separator). Preserve the separator and other background. Demos: (1) 17x22, horizontal separator row3, singleton color5 at row10 col16 moved to row4 col16, with full row5 color8. (2) vertical separator col20, color4 object just left, full color8 col17, on far side of object; object already adjacent to separator. (3) vertical separator col12, color3 shape on right shifted left until its nearest side is adjacent to separator, with full color8 line one cell beyond the moved shape. (4) separator col0, color6 block at cols4-5 shifts to cols1-2, full col3 color8. Test: horizontal separator row15, color7 irregular shape rows7-12 shifted down by2 to rows9-14, original removed; full row8 color8. Two wrong attempts retained the original object while adding its shifted copy, or drew the line adjacent to original rather than moving the object; correct operation is MOVE, not copy, and put line beyond shifted object. For horizontal orientation, shift rows; for vertical, shift columns. Use color8 as line and preserve original separator color2.",
 "global_": true,
